<p>
  A template is a document you have set up once &mdash; the file, the fields
  and who fills in each one &mdash; so that sending it again takes seconds.
  Templates and folders are unlimited on both plans.
</p>

<h2>Making a template</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Upload a PDF or a Word file from your dashboard, or open one of the starter templates that come with a new account and edit it.</li>
  <li>Name the parties. A contract might have a "Client" and a "Contractor"; every field you place belongs to one of them.</li>
  <li>Drag fields onto the page and drop them where they go. Resize a field by its corner, and move it with the arrow keys for fine work.</li>
  <li>Mark the fields that must be filled in as required.</li>
  <li>Save. The template now sits on your dashboard, ready to send.</li>
</ol>

<h2>The fields you can place</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Signature</strong> and <strong>Initials</strong> &mdash; drawn, typed or uploaded by the signer.</li>
  <li><strong>Text</strong>, <strong>Number</strong> and <strong>Cells</strong> &mdash; free typing, figures, and boxed characters for things like a reference number.</li>
  <li><strong>Date</strong> &mdash; a date picker, so nobody types one in the wrong order.</li>
  <li><strong>Checkbox</strong>, <strong>Multiple choice</strong>, <strong>Radio</strong> and <strong>Select</strong> &mdash; the ways to offer a choice.</li>
  <li><strong>File</strong> and <strong>Image</strong> &mdash; for a document or a photo the signer has to attach.</li>
  <li><strong>Stamp</strong> &mdash; a company stamp or seal the signer applies.</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Any field can be made read-only or given a default value, so you can pre-fill
  what you already know and leave the signer only what they have to decide.
</p>

<h2>Keeping templates tidy</h2>

<p>
  Group templates into folders, rename them, and archive the ones you have
  finished with. Archiving hides a template but keeps its files &mdash; and
  those files still count towards your storage. Only
  <strong>delete permanently</strong>, from the archived list, actually frees
  the space, and deleting a template permanently takes the documents made from
  it as well.
</p>

<aside class="help-callout">
  <p>
    <strong>Good to know:</strong> saving a template costs you nothing.
    Templates and folders are unlimited on both plans, and the starter
    templates a new account is given never spend a send or a completion. Only
    sending a document for signature is counted &mdash; see
    <%= link_to 'Free plan limits', help_article_path('free-plan-limits') %>.
  </p>
</aside>

<h2>Sending from a template</h2>

<p>
  Open the template, choose <strong>Send</strong>, and fill in who is playing
  each part. The fields and the order come with it. The original template is
  never changed by sending it, so the same one serves every client you have.
</p>

<p>
  Paid accounts can also add conditional logic, so a field or a whole page only
  appears when an earlier answer calls for it.
</p>

<p>
  Next: <%= link_to 'Sending a document', help_article_path('sending-a-document') %>
  or <%= link_to 'Getting started', help_article_path('getting-started') %>.
</p>
